{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>יחן.</b> Of the doubled-form verbs, like על כמון יוסב (Isaiah 28:24). The meaning is that HaShem shows favor to the wicked, yet he does not learn righteousness — the meaning being that He extends [patience] to him, perhaps he will learn." "<b>בארץ נכוחות.</b> In a place where there is uprightness, they commit injustice." "<b>נכוחות.</b> From the root נכח, like טובים ונכוחים (2 Samuel 15:3). And he does not set his heart to see the grandeur of HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:14.398456482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}